     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I am conducting a path analysis with 4 variables. The schematic can be seen below:</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/attach/1d7b9164ca561/path_model.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"path_model.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"190\" border=\"0\"></a><br></p><p></p><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m interested in both the direct and indirect effects. I created the following syntax for the effects of PAG on AUDIT<br></div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">active</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;<br>PSP ~ p1*PAG + mOFC<br><br>AUDIT ~ p2*PAG + p3*mOFC + p5*PSP<br><br>total := p1 + p2*p5 + p3*p5 <br>indirect := p2*p5 + p3*p5   <br>&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br><br>active</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">active</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">active</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>I could do the same thing for the effects of mOFC but I don&#39;t know how to incorporate <u>both</u> PAG and mOFC in the same model. I tried:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">active</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;<br>PSP ~ p1*PAG + mOFC<br>PSP ~ p4*mOFC + PAG<br><br><br>AUDIT ~ p2*PAG + p3*mOFC + p5*PSP<br><br><br>total := p1 + p4 + p2*p5 + p3*p5 <br>indirect := p2*p5 + p3*p5   <br>&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br><br><br>active</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">active</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">active</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>This, rather obviously, produces an error of duplicate model element for PSP. Could anyone help? Thank you so much!</div><div><br></div></div>"
